# shell: both
# work: home
# FS-060: the Trash is a move like any other, so an item cut and then
# trashed is still on the clipboard -- under the name it has in there.
wait 6
note a.txt is cut, and then trashed before anything is pasted
click-row 1
wait 3
key x ctrl
wait 3
key Delete
wait 5
expect-alert cannot be reverted
key m
wait 30
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/a.txt
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/a.txt
note the entry went into the Trash with it, so pasting where it came from
note brings it back rather than finding nothing to paste
key v ctrl
wait 40
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/a.txt
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/a.txt
quit
